      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CORMORAN STRIKE NZ (6) was runner-up to race rival Gandhi Mail last start but had beaten that rival when winning his previous two outings here and starts 10m in front of him at the handicap so can turn the tables. GANDHI MAIL (12) won for the second time in four Australian outings when he led from a wide barrier and proved too strong last start. Has to overcome a 20m handicap this time but could be ready to go right on with the job. PESCO POLLO (11) has ground to make up on the top-two selections through recent attempts but scored back-to-back wins here last month, one from a standing start, and he steps up to a distance where he owns a good strike rate. SPEEDY LOVER (10) can be competitive again having placed in three of his last four starts including a second the last time he attempted a standing start.",
